\label{tab:sensitivity_b2}
\small
\setlength{\tabcolsep}{5pt}
\begin{tabular}{@{}lcccccccc@{}}
\toprule
Threshold & TP & FP & FN & TN & Accuracy [95\% CI] & Precision & Recall & F1 \\
\midrule
$\geq 1.0\times$ & 3 & 2 & 0 & 3 & 75.0\% \; [34.9, 96.8] & 60.0\% & 100\% & 75.0\% \\
$\geq 1.2\times$ & 3 & 1 & 0 & 4 & 87.5\% \; [47.3, 99.7] & 75.0\% & 100\% & 85.7\% \\
\rowcolor{gray!15}
$\geq 1.5\times$ & 3 & 1 & 0 & 4 & 87.5\% \; [47.3, 99.7] & 75.0\% & 100\% & 85.7\% \\
$\geq 1.7\times$ & 2 & 1 & 1 & 4 & 75.0\% \; [34.9, 96.8] & 66.7\% & 66.7\% & 66.7\% \\
$\geq 2.0\times$ & 2 & 1 & 1 & 4 & 75.0\% \; [34.9, 96.8] & 66.7\% & 66.7\% & 66.7\% \\
$\geq 3.9\times$ & 2 & 0 & 1 & 5 & 87.5\% \; [47.3, 99.7] & 100\% & 66.7\% & 80.0\% \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{table*}

\subsection{Threshold Recommendation}

For the main diagnostic (Task~B2), we recommend $\nve \geq 1.5\times$ as the operating threshold for three reasons:

\begin{enumerate}[nosep,leftmargin=*]
\item \textbf{Maximum recall.} The $1.5\times$ threshold achieves 100\% recall, detecting all three CIVO cases including the transient case (009b, $\nve = 1.62\times$). Raising the threshold to $1.7\times$ loses 009b, dropping recall to 66.7\%.
\item \textbf{Best F1.} At $1.5\times$, F1 = 85.7\%, the highest among all tested thresholds for B2. The single false positive (008e\_v3\_s2) is mechanistically identifiable as IRD rather than CIVO.
\item \textbf{Sensitivity--specificity tradeoff.} Lower thresholds ($1.0\times$) add false positives without gaining true positives. Higher thresholds ($\geq 1.7\times$) sacrifice recall without eliminating the 008e\_v3\_s2 false positive (which requires $\tau > 3.78$).
\end{enumerate}

For Task~B1 (sustained CIVO only), perfect classification is achievable at $\nve \geq 3.9\times$, but with only $n_{\text{pos}} = 2$ the statistical power is severely limited (accuracy 95\% CI: [63.1\%, 100\%]).

\paragraph{Limitations.} With $n = 8$ experiments, all Clopper-Pearson confidence intervals are wide (e.g., 87.5\% accuracy has 95\% CI [47.3\%, 99.7\%]). These results should be interpreted as a diagnostic proof-of-concept rather than a validated clinical threshold. Replication across additional environments and seeds is needed to establish tighter bounds.

